A||N||12||rockcrawl||My GT got beat by a 2M4 !!!!!||||4||
Z||000000||rockcrawl||11-17-2000||10:42 PM||||I just finished putting a rebuilt engine in my '87 GT auto last week. It's stock except for a .030 overbore. When I got it together I thought it seemed a little sluggish, but my previous Fiero was a 3.8 4spd and I haven't driven a 2.8 for a few years. My buddy and I were out racing around tonite just having some fun with our Fieros. I found out that my car tops out at 90 mph with the pedal floored, and when we lined up a a traffic light and raced from a stop, he had several car lengths on me by the time I hit 60, and I never caught up. His car is a stock '86 2M4 5spd (I sold it to him). I can't believe the auto trans is slowing me down that much, there must be some other problem. I suspect the catalitic converter is partially blocked. I can hear it rattling when I start the car.<P>One thing is for sure though, I can loose him in the curves! His 185/75/14s don't corner very well!!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||4
Z||000001||My7Fieros||11-17-2000||10:46 PM||||I suspect you've def got a prob w/ your engine then..escpecially if it only tops out at 90 mph. I dont know how many miles you've got on your rebuild, but I'd give it a good break in period before engaging in any sort of racing activity.<p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 11-17-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||rockcrawl||11-17-2000||10:57 PM||||The engine has 12k miles on it already so it's well broken-in by now. I pulled it out of my '86 that got a 3800 swap. I normally do not partake in any type of street racing, but for some reason I was feeling rebelious tonite. I think it had something to do with having more than one Fiero in the same place at the same time.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Patrick's Dad||11-17-2000||11:30 PM||||Put the rear end up on jack stands (Or the whole thing) and knock on your catalytic converter (When it's cool). If you can hear stuff rattling around in there, this can be singly responsible for your lack of performance. If it's just rattling around under your butt, then I'd tend to think that it's something else....<P>Of course, other things may be ganging up on you, but this is the one that you mentioned.||||reg||1
Z||000004||GT Bastard||11-18-2000||01:49 AM||||Fierogod says: "Silly rabbit, you're only running on 1/2 of your injectors.  It'll run smooth as butter on 3 injectors(1 bank or the other.)"||||reg||1
Z||000005||N_Man||11-18-2000||01:57 AM||||im a fan of the clogged cat idea<P>A frind of mine has a GT and he litterally walked away from me, chopped the cat now its the other way around.<P>But before the rebuild my engine went through oil so it was the likly culprit||||reg||1
Z||000006||hugh||11-18-2000||08:18 AM||||A long time ago I had a bad convertor in my Caddy and I could outrun it on foot for about 50 yards.My service truck convertor went bad,same thing.Punched it out and it was like changing the engine.||||reg||1
Z||000007||fropuff||11-18-2000||02:43 PM||||I should try that on my Cutlass.  It gets BAD acceleration.  Can't outrun it on foot, but it gets 0-60 in about 25.  Not good for me.  I should look into that when I get the exhaust hole fixed. <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000008||fldevel||11-18-2000||02:47 PM||||yikes .. i dont think ive ever had the nerve to top my car out .. but i would suspect it to top out at about 125 r so maybe more .. i know ive had it up to 100 and had quite a bit more pedel to go ... as for your lil prob i would agree with the cat problem .. *NOTE* a cherry bomb is perfect length to replace the cat||||reg||1
Z||000009||jerpro||11-18-2000||03:27 PM||||well... the reaon you got beat by a 2m4 is because they are better. Don't get me wrong I own a 84 2m4 and a 87 v6. I personally enjoy the 2m4 better. Although a smaller engine, It has a lot of potential. If it is prepped up appropiatedly (and you take two spark plugs out of the v6)<P>------------------<BR>Only try your best, and if you don't succeed... TRY HARDER.||||reg||1
Z||000010||rockcrawl||11-18-2000||07:04 PM||||Well, I hollowed out the cat today and that was definately at least part of the problem. It's still no powerhouse, but I think I could at least beat the 2M4 now. There were big chunks of catalyst just bouncing around in there. It wasn't totally blocked, but enough to affect performance. It also has a weird hollow note to the exhaust now, almost like the Flowmaster sound. I left the thing in place so that it would at least pass the visual emissions inspection. <P>Several years ago I had an '87 GT auto that I got up to 120mph, but it had 195/50/15 tires so I wasn't really going that fast.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000011||Fformula88||11-18-2000||08:14 PM||||Thos pesky cats!  Mine is also partially clogged.  Every now and then I have to beat it up with a hammer to get it cleared out.  Its full of dirt.  The previous owner of the car did just about zero maintainance on the car.  When I got it the engine was running very rich, and I think it destroyed the inside of it.  I am gonna replace it all in the spring!<P>Try going over all the vacumn lines too.  I found a split elbow in one of mine going to the throttle.  After fixing it ran better and gave me a bit more power.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">  <BR>1988 Fiero Formula||||reg||1
Z||000012||hugh||11-18-2000||09:28 PM||||My truck has that hollow sound also.Could some of the convertor have gotten into your muffler?||||reg||1
